INT. PEST-CONTROL TRAINING SEMINAR - HOTEL BALLROOM - DAY

Folding chairs. A projector screen with a photograph of a cockroach the size of a thumb. A tray of lukewarm danishes. Two chairs are occupied.

AUGUSTUS "HUMPHREY" BRANDYWINE-OYELOWO (50s, rumpled blazer, lanyard) is trying to open a danish with the ferocity of a man defusing a bomb.

In the next chair, PRISCILLA "PRIZZY" DELACROIX-NAKASHIMA (30s, crisp polo, notebook) is writing in a hand so neat it looks typeset.

At the front, nobody. The presenter has not arrived. The cockroach on the screen stares at the room with enormous composure.

HUMPHREY
Prizzy, I think we've been had.

PRIZZY
Humphrey, we paid for the seminar.

HUMPHREY
We paid for a seminar. We didn't pay for an absence.

PRIZZY
I'm sure he's coming.

HUMPHREY
It's been forty minutes. I've eaten two danishes. I have regrets.

PRIZZY
(muttering)
Regrets, he says.

A pause. Humphrey looks at the screen. At the cockroach.

HUMPHREY
That's a lot of bug.

PRIZZY
That's an American cockroach.

HUMPHREY
Is it? It looks Greek.

PRIZZY
Humphrey.

HUMPHREY
It's got the look. Stately. Doomed.

Prizzy puts down her pen. Humphrey takes a bite of danish.

HUMPHREY (CONT'D)
(to the empty room)
Anyone?

The empty room does not answer. A fluorescent tube buzzes.

PRIZZY
I could present.

HUMPHREY
You could.

PRIZZY
I know all the slides. I've seen the deck.

HUMPHREY
You have the deck?

PRIZZY
It's on my laptop.

HUMPHREY
Prizzy, that's the bravest thing anyone's said since the continental breakfast.

She stands. Smooths her polo. Walks to the front. Plugs in the cable. The projector flickers, then flares to life with a new slide: a diagram of a roach's digestive tract.

PRIZZY
(to the room)
Good morning, everyone.

HUMPHREY
(whispering to himself)
Oh, this is going to be good.

Prizzy clears her throat, takes a breath. The door at the back bangs in the wind, and nobody comes in.

Humphrey slumps. Prizzy continues, regardless.

PRIZZY (CONT'D)
(to the empty doorway, kindly)
We're in the middle of a seminar.

HUMPHREY
Prizzy, let the draft in. It might be the roaches.
